## DEVIATION D-S2-1 (recorded 2026-08-15, BEFORE any Stage-2 fit result existed)

PREREG §3 stated the config diff vs s2.D.cum.b0-6.json would be 'exactly one key:
label'. That turned out to be IMPOSSIBLE, and G1 caught it on its first run.

resolve_featureset(B1..B6, extras) on TODAY's blocks.py returns 247 columns, not the
241 the benchmark used: the B2 item-observability index (6 cols) was added to
blocks.py AFTER the canonical fit ran on 2026-08-12. The v1 training frame does not
carry them, so the canonical config no longer loads against its own frame:
  ValueError: frame is missing requested columns
  ['b2_item_observability_status', 'b2_n_prior_days_items_observed', ...] (6 total)

=> The canonical s2.D.cum.b0-6 fit is NOT reproducible today from its own config.
This independently confirms NY_COMPARISON_AUDIT_2026_08_15.md finding S-1 and uses
its prescribed recovery: intersect the resolved set with the frame schema.

  resolved today       : 247
  available in v1 pair : 241   <- matches banked n_features exactly
  missing from v1      : 6     <- exactly the B2 item-observability index

All three Stage-2 configs therefore pin featureset=[] and extra_columns=<explicit
241, in benchmark order>. The three differ from EACH OTHER only in 'label', so the
target remains the only difference between the control and the B3/M1 arms. Whether
the reconstruction is faithful to the BANKED benchmark is exactly what G1 tests.

