## G1 OUTCOME + MEASURED REFIT NUISANCE (2026-08-15, before the B3 read)

G1 null-change control (sev.CTRL, label y_final, copied frames, seed 101):
  AUROC 0.7133278601031884  vs banked 0.7133041237871912   ABS DIFF 2.374e-05
  quantization 'unavailable:CatBoostError' == benchmark's string   n_features 241
  rung_rows 755389 == banked.  Pre-registered band |d| < 1e-4 => PASS, proceed.

NOT bit-exact, and the cause is NOT a numerical epsilon: comparing the control's
predictions to the banked ones gives corr 0.9937, max|dp| 0.265, mean|dp| 0.0096,
and ZERO identical predictions. A nominally-identical refit produces a MATERIALLY
DIFFERENT MODEL with equivalent ranking.

That makes sev.CTRL a planted null control. Measured refit nuisance, by label:
  T0  +2.37e-05     B3  -6.87e-04     M1  -2.36e-04     S1  +7.47e-05
  B3 nuisance 95% CI [-9.89e-04, -3.76e-04] -- EXCLUDES ZERO.

=> A pure refit, with no target change and no substrate change, yields a
'statistically significant' B3 effect. This is STAGE2_INFERENCE_RULE_FINAL:227
demonstrated directly on this experiment rather than cited, and it vindicates
PREREG SS5's decision to exclude 'CI excludes zero' from the gate.

It also validates the imported sigma: |nuisance| 6.87e-04 = 0.8x the on-surface
sigma-hat 8.61e-04 used for MDE(k=1). The +0.005 trigger sits ~7x above it.

CONSEQUENCE for reporting: the pre-registered primary (B3-trained vs BANKED frozen)
carries this nuisance. A matched secondary (B3-trained vs sev.CTRL, both on copied
frames, same seed/environment, target the ONLY difference) is better controlled and
will be reported alongside -- labelled, NOT substituted for the primary.

